:''For the enemy encountered in the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]], see [[Mass Production EVA (Enemy)]].''
'''Mass Production EVA''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event/Gacha Drop|Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]]. It was added in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 814
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Mass Production EVA
|name2 = Mass Production EVA-Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mass Production EVA-Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Mass Production EVA's most notable characteristics are its somewhat low cost and especially short recharge time, being just over 30 seconds. These are comparable to a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]], but the unit has the stats and abilities of an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Super Rare]].

That said, its ability uptime and activation rate tend to fall short on their own, and a large portion of its potential relies on you stacking multiple Mass Production EVAs. In stages where cash is plentiful, this can be a non-issue, and its performance with two or three of them on the field is almost enough to permanently [[Freeze]] even the most threatening target traits (if you're not painfully unlucky).

Mass Production EVA's matchups are equally very impressive, as it outranges almost every relevant [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] threat—from [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] to [[Winged Pigge]]—and its [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] lets it counter even [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]]. Given how many [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless enemies]] tend to use and abuse [[Wave Attack]]s, Mass Production EVA can stall these threats with relative ease under the right conditions. Its status as a backliner and acceptable HP/knockback count give it phenomenal survivability for its cost, more than enough to stack even four of them at any given moment.

The main issue with Mass Production EVA is its cost over time. 2,700¢ is not cheap; just three of them on the field will cost you 8,100¢ over the course of 100 seconds. A large portion of its utility lies in stacking, which severely hinders its potential in cash-tight stages where threats spawn on a timer rather than on base hit. This means Mass Production EVA should mainly be used in stages that give you ample time to prepare, since its speed is slow enough to prevent it from rushing toward the enemy base.

{{Job|Classification = Backliner & Crowd-Controller}}

